    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe TUI disables title updates when terminfo omits `tsl` or `fsl`, although modern terminals generally support the xterm-compatible OSC 0 title sequence.\n\n## Solution\n\nAfter applying terminal-specific workarounds, fill missing `tsl`/`fsl` with OSC 0 and BEL for all terminals except hterm. Existing terminfo and terminal-specific values remain unchanged.\n\nAdd a functional test that supplies terminfo without title capabilities and verifies `titlestring` updates the terminal title.\n\nCloses #20706.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-08-16T11:25:56Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "The terminfo entry already has this (at least in ncurses 6.6-2), so it works without these code changes. MacOS doesn't ship with the terminfo, but users can add it if necessary if they want to set TERM to wezterm. It also works if TERM=xterm-256color, which is the default on wezterm.\r\n\r\nIf TERM=wezterm and the user doesn't have terminfo for wezterm, the term gets set to ansi anyways, so a bunch of other stuff would be broken.\r\n\r\nIn brief, I don't think this is needed.",
            "created_at": "2026-08-11T22:24:02Z",
